config VIDEO_HISI_JPGD
	tristate "HiSilicon JPEG decoder (JPGD) mem2mem driver"
	depends on V4L_MEM2MEM_DRIVERS
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	depends on ARCH_HISI_BVT || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF
	depends on PM
	select VIDEOBUF2_DMA_CONTIG
	select V4L2_MEM2MEM_DEV
	select V4L2_JPEG_HELPER
	help
	  Support for the baseline JPEG decoder (JPGD) of the HiSilicon
	  Hi3520D V100 and Hi3536D V100 SoCs. The driver is a V4L2
	  memory-to-memory device: a complete JPEG file goes in, a
	  semi-planar YUV picture (NV21, NV61, NV42 or GREY, optionally
	  reduced by 2, 4 or 8) comes out. Progressive, arithmetic coded,
	  12 bit and CMYK files are refused.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called hisi-jpgd.
